---
/**
 * Home.
 *
 * Layout order is the argument (the dir.co.jp lesson, scaled to a one-product
 * shop): identity in half a breath, then the flagship IN the hero doing its
 * actual job, then the product grid, and only then the philosophy. The
 * previous layout led with two screens of prose and read as a blog; a visitor
 * must learn what is for sale before they are asked to care why.
 *
 * Two rules kept from the first version, because they are what make the page
 * credible:
 *
 *   1. No invented proof. No customer logos, no "trusted by", no metrics that
 *      do not exist, no team page for one person. The NEWS strip carries real
 *      dated facts only.
 *   2. Say the unflattering thing where it is true. One product ships and one
 *      does not, and the page says which before it asks for anything.
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import ProductCard from '../components/ProductCard.astro';

const products = (await getCollection('products')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);

const title = 'Joseki — known-good moves for agentic work';
const description =
  'Joseki builds toolkits for agentic engineering work. Clawform, safe CloudFormation workflows for Claude Code, is the first.';

const CLAWFORM = 'https://clawform.thejoseki.com';

// Real dates, real releases — the strip earns its place only while every line
// is a checkable fact. Newest first, keep to three.
const NEWS = [
  { date: '2026-07-27', text: 'Clawform 2.2.0 — the content kit is now delivered only after a licence check', href: CLAWFORM },
  { date: '2026-07-27', text: 'Free 14-day Clawform trial opens — full kit, no card', href: CLAWFORM },
  { date: '2026-07-26', text: 'Team licence: ten devices on one key, $299 one-time', href: `${CLAWFORM}/#pricing` },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Section grid={true}>
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Joseki</p>
        <h1>Known-good moves for agentic&nbsp;work.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          In Go, a <em>joseki</em> is a sequence studied until it is known to be
          sound. We build that for the engineering work an agent does — the
          studied part, so the agent's speed is worth having.
        </p>
        <p class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-accent" href="#products">What we sell</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="mailto:support@thejoseki.com">Get in touch</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!--
        The flagship, above the fold, shown WORKING rather than described: the
        one thing a stranger must leave with is "this company sells Clawform,
        and this is what it does". The terminal excerpt is the hook's real
        output, verbatim from the product site.
      -->
      <aside class="spotlight" aria-label="Clawform — flagship product">
        <p class="spot-kicker">Flagship — on sale now</p>
        <h2 class="spot-name">Clawform</h2>
        <p class="spot-tag">Safe CloudFormation workflows for Claude Code</p>

        <figure class="spot-term" aria-label="Example: the hook blocking a destructive command">
          <div class="spot-term-head" aria-hidden="true">
            <span></span><span></span><span></span>
            <p>claude code · PreToolUse hook</p>
          </div>
          <pre>$ aws cloudformation delete-stack --stack-name p-acme-billing-rds
<span class="t-block">✗ blocked by Clawform — exit 2, the command never ran</span></pre>
        </figure>

        <p class="spot-trial">Free 14-day trial — full kit, no card.</p>
        <p class="spot-price">Then $49 per seat · $299 per team · one-time</p>

        <p class="spot-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-accent" href={CLAWFORM}>Try Clawform free</a>
          <a class="spot-docs" href={`${CLAWFORM}/docs/`}>Docs</a>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <!-- dir.co.jp's NEWS pattern at one-person scale: dated, checkable, three lines. -->
    <ul class="news" aria-label="News">
      {NEWS.map((n) => (
        <li>
          <span class="news-date">{n.date}</span>
          <a href={n.href}>{n.text}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section id="products" tone="paper">
    <p class="eyebrow">Products</p>
    <h2>One shipped. One still early.</h2>
    <p class="lead lead-paper">
      Clawform is on sale. ClaudeBrew is not, and its card says which parts
      exist rather than implying the rest are close.
    </p>

    <div class="grid">
      {products.map((entry) => <ProductCard entry={entry} />)}
    </div>

    <p class="lead lead-paper roadmap-line">
      Both are early versions of something wider. The pattern — rules read
      before writing, tools that make the real change reviewable, guards that
      refuse the irreversible — does not depend on AWS, on CloudFormation, or
      on Claude Code. Other clouds, other infrastructure languages and other
      agents are where this goes. <strong>No dates</strong>: a schedule from a
      one-person shop is a guess wearing a calendar. Buy what works today.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="why">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why toolkits</p>
    <h2>An agent's confidence is not evidence.</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        A model that writes infrastructure, or a migration, or a release, is
        genuinely fast — and it is exactly as fluent when it is wrong. The
        output looks the same either way. That is the whole problem: the
        failure mode is not gibberish you would catch, it is something
        plausible you would not.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prompting harder does not fix that, because the thing missing is not
        instruction. What is missing is the part a careful engineer supplies
        without being asked — knowing which move is safe here, refusing the one
        that is not, and stopping to show you the diff before it lands.
      </p>
      <p>
        So we build that part: rules an agent reads before it writes, tools
        that make the real change deterministic and reviewable, and guards that
        refuse the commands nobody should run by accident. Each tool states
        what it does not cover, because a safety claim you cannot keep is worse
        than none.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="paper-2">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
    <h2>One address, answered by a person.</h2>
    <p class="lead lead-paper">
      No form, no list, no sequence of emails you did not ask for. If you want
      to know when something ships, or whether it would fit what you run, write
      and say so.
    </p>
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-dark" href="mailto:support@thejoseki.com">support@thejoseki.com</a>
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--fs-hero);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.04;
    color: var(--on-ink-strong);
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--on-ink-strong);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    max-width: 24ch;
  }
  :global(.on-paper) h2 { color: var(--on-paper); }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 380px), 1fr));
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--on-ink-muted);
    max-width: 54ch;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .lead em { color: var(--on-ink-strong); font-style: italic; }
  .lead-paper { color: var(--on-paper-muted); margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .roadmap-line { font-size: var(--fs-base); max-width: 62ch; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 0; }
  .roadmap-line strong { color: var(--on-paper); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ── Flagship spotlight ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .spotlight {
    background: var(--ink-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    padding: 26px 28px 28px;
  }
  .spot-kicker {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .spot-name {
    font-size: var(--fs-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--on-ink-strong);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .spot-tag {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--on-ink-muted);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .spot-term {
    background: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .spot-term-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .spot-term-head span {
    width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .spot-term-head span:first-child { background: var(--accent); }
  .spot-term-head p {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    color: var(--on-ink-muted);
    margin-left: 6px;
  }
  .spot-term pre {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--on-ink);
    padding: 12px 14px;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  .t-block { color: var(--accent); }

  .spot-trial {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--on-ink-strong);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .spot-price {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--on-ink-muted);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .spot-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .spot-docs {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--on-ink-muted);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .spot-docs:hover { color: var(--on-ink-strong); }

  /* ── News strip ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .news {
    margin-top: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 18px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .news li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .news-date {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    color: var(--on-ink-muted);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .news a {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--on-ink);
  }
  .news a:hover { color: var(--on-ink-strong); text-decoration: underline; }

  .prose { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .prose p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--on-ink-muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 320px), 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; align-items: center; }
  .btn-dark { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
  .btn-dark:hover { background: var(--ink-3); }
</style>
